From c291ab21aa810b8052349da469baf531a13ea95b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Heiwad Osman <4895017+heiwad@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:43:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dsv41): KV pool room from the display reservation
 (TF_DS_DISPLAY_KV_MIB)

When TF_DS_DISPLAY_KV_MIB is set to a multiple of 16 up to 2032, each rank grows its KV pool capacity by the positions those bytes fund and carves the first pool planes from one contiguous UVA span backed by an ordinary host mapping and a DRM dumb buffer on /dev/dri/card0 registered with cuMemHostRegister_v2. Fails closed if a display connector is connected or any DRM, mmap or CUDA registration step fails. Spanned plane clears split at the registration cut and kept-row moves on spanned planes run through ops.copyRows. Off by default with identical behaviour.
